  "details": "In the current \"Create Instance\" UI, the Enable Queue checkbox for group instances is not checked by default, or if previously disabled remembers this setting. This leads to many group instances being created without a queue, which is sub-optimal in most use cases.\n\nQueues are particularly important in public group instances of game or social worlds, where capping out is extremely common. Without queues, joining capped instances becomes a frustrating experience of constantly checking player numbers, fighting client cache TTL, and moderators often struggle to get in to instances because of it. In the case of public game groups it is not always staff creating these instances, but rather random group members and in almost all known cases, enabling the queue provides a better user experience.\n\nThis seems to be more an issue of users overlooking the option or misunderstanding it, not because they genuinely want it disabled / have made an informed decision.\n\nSuggestion:\n\n1) Please change the UI so that Enable Queue is checked by default when creating a group instance, regardless of prior settings. Users can still manually uncheck it if they need to, but this choice should *always* be non-default.\n\n2) Consider giving group owners the ability to enforce queues where they wish to do so.",
